<div id="pf1f" class="pf w0 h0" data-page-no="1f"><div class="pc pc1f w0 h0"><img class="bi x0 y0 w1 h1" alt="" src="data:image/png;base64,"/><div class="c x1 y65 w2 hb"><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y25c ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">navigate an or<span class="_ _1"></span>ganization, scope and gather requirements, control costs, and</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y25d ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">continuously learn will set you apart from the data engineers who rely</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y25e ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">solely on their technical abilities to carry their career<span class="_ _2"></span>.</div><div class="t m0 x6 hc y25f ff7 fs4 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">T<span class="_ _6"></span>echnical Responsibilities</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y260 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">At a high level, you must understand how to build architectures that</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y261 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">optimize performance and cost, whether the components are prepackaged or</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y262 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">homegrown. Ultimately<span class="_ _2"></span>, architectures and constituent technologies are</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y263 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">building blocks to serve the data engineering lifecycle. Recall the stages of</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y264 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">the data engineering lifecycle (<span class="fc2">Figure 1-3</span>):</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y265 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Data generation</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y266 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Data ingestion</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y267 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Data storage</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y268 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Data transformation</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y269 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Serving data</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y26a ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">The undercurrents of the data engineering lifecycle are:</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y26b ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Data management</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y26c ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">DataOps</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y26d ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Data architecture</div><div class="t m0 x8 h5 y26e ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Software engineering</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y26f ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">Zooming in a bit, we discuss some of the tactical data and technology skills</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y270 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">you’ll need as a data engineer here; we will discuss these in much more</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y271 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">detail in subsequent chapters.</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y272 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">People often ask—should a data engineer know how to code? Short answer</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y273 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">—yes. A data engineer should have production-grade software engineering</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y274 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">chops. W<span class="_ _2"></span>e note that the nature of software development projects undertaken</div><div class="t m0 x6 h5 y275 ff8 fs2 fc0 sc0 ls0 ws0">by data engineers has changed fundamentally in the last few years. A great</div></div><a class="l" href="#pfe" data-dest-detail='[14,"XYZ",76.5,720,null]'><div class="d m1" style="border-style:none;position:absolute;left:428.921618px;bottom:851.715686px;width:63.000000px;height:16.500000px;background-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.000001);"></div></a></div><div class="pi" data-data='{"ctm":[1.633987,0.000000,0.000000,1.633987,0.000000,0.000000]}'></div></div>
